layout "layout.faqir"

block content
  p
    | The
    strong Floor
    | is Buildyboy's home screen. It answers one question at a glance: what are all my Claude Code sessions doing right
    | now, and does any of them need me? Open it with
    strong Floor
    | in the top bar (or the first tab at the bottom of a phone).
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="floor-desktop.png" alt="The Floor in canvas view: a bay per machine, each holding session cards with a lamp, a status, an activity line, three meters and a conveyor belt of tool calls." caption="The canvas view on a computer. Amber cards are waiting for you.")

  h2#attention-bar The attention bar
  p
    | The strip at the very top of every page summarises what needs you. It appears only when there is something to say,
    | and turns amber with a pulsing dot when a session is waiting or a job has failed. It can show:
  ul
    li
      code N waiting for you
      | : sessions waiting in the last 24 hours, plus open Inbox cards.
    li
      code N job(s) failed
      | : jobs that failed or lost contact in the last 24 hours.
    li
      code N stale
      | : sessions that stopped reporting while working.
    li
      code Walk mode on
      | and
      code Everything paused
      | : reminders that these global switches are on.
  p
    | Tap the bar to jump to the
    a(href="/docs/inbox") Inbox
    | .
  +callout(variant="muted")
    @content
      p
        | The
        code Walk mode on
        | reminder only reflects the global switch in the Inbox. Walk mode turned on for a single machine or a single
        | session does not show here; that session's own header says
        strong walk mode
        | instead.

  h2#bays-and-stations Bays and stations
  p
    | Each paired computer is a
    strong bay
    | , drawn as a dashed box. Its header shows a green dot when the machine is online (it sent something in the last 5
    | minutes, or its runner is connected), its name, how many sessions are waiting, and a line with its platform,
    | whether the runner is online, and how many stations it holds.
  p
    | Each session is a
    strong station
    | : a card with everything you need to judge it without opening it.
  ol
    li
      strong The lamp
      | (the coloured circle) shows the status. Green pulsing is working, amber pulsing is waiting on you, steady blue is
      | idle, slowly pulsing blue is compacting, amber and grey stripes is stale, red is an error and grey is ended. The
      | whole card glows amber while it waits for you, and ended cards are dimmed.
    li
      strong The project
      | in capitals, and under it the git branch (
      code ⎇ main
      | ). An amber dot after the branch means there are uncommitted changes;
      code no git
      | means the folder is not a git repository.
    li
      strong The status word
      | on the right, such as
      code WAITING ON YOU
      | or
      code IDLE
      | .
    li
      strong The session name
      | (or "Untitled session").
    li
      strong The activity line
      | after
      code ▸
      | says what it is doing right now, for example
      code Bash: npm test
      | ,
      code Editing server/db.ts
      | ,
      code Proposing a plan
      | or
      code Waiting for prompt
      | . While a session waits for you, the line shows Claude Code's own message in amber instead.
    li
      strong Three meters.
      code Context
      | is a small tank showing how full the conversation's context window is (blue, then amber from 75% and red from 90%;
      | a dash means unknown).
      code Cost
      | is the session's spend so far in dollars.
      code Time
      | is how long ago the session started.
    li
      strong The conveyor belt
      | at the bottom shows the last 20 tool calls, oldest on the left. Each block is coloured by kind: blue for reading
      | and searching files, violet for edits, orange for shell commands, teal for web access, pink for MCP tools, yellow
      | for subagents and grey for anything else. A block that is still running pulses; a failed, denied or interrupted
      | one is dimmed with a red outline. Hover a block to see the tool and its result. An empty belt says
      code belt idle
      | .
  p
    | Small circles marked
    code ✣
    | floating above a station are its
    strong subagents
    | (helpers Claude started). They fade away shortly after they finish. On the phone list they appear as chips.
  +callout(variant="info")
    @content
      p
        | The context meter is most accurate with the optional statusline bridge switched on. Without it, many sessions
        | show a dash. See
        a(href="/docs/settings#telemetry") Telemetry and statusline
        | .
  p
    | The
    code Time
    | meter keeps counting while a session sits idle, so a session you left open this morning can show many hours. That
    | is time since start, not time spent working.

  h2#views Canvas and list
  p
    | Switch between the two views with
    strong List
    | and
    strong Canvas
    | at the top right. Phones start in the list, larger screens in the canvas. The choice is not remembered between visits.
  h3#canvas The canvas
  ul
    li Drag the background to move around; use the + and − buttons (or your trackpad) to zoom; the frame button fits everything on screen.
    li Drag a bay to move it, or drag a station inside its bay. Positions are remembered in this browser.
    li
      strong Reset layout
      | (top right) puts everything back in its automatic place.
    li Click a station, or focus it with Tab and press Enter, to open the session.
  h3#list The list
  p
    | The list groups sessions by machine under a header with the online dot, the machine name and whether its runner is
    | on. Cards are full width; tap one to open the session.
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="floor-phone.png" alt="The Floor on a phone: the List view with a machine header and full-width session cards." caption="On a phone the Floor is a list, most urgent first." phone)

  h2#filters Filters
  p The row under the title narrows what you see. Your choices are remembered in this browser.
  ul
    li
      strong Live
      | : sessions that have not ended and have done something in the last 24 hours.
    li
      strong Today
      | (the default): sessions with activity since midnight.
    li
      strong All
      | : the 200 most recent sessions, ended ones included.
    li
      strong All projects
      | and
      strong All machines
      | : pick one project or one machine.
  p
    | The counters next to the title (for example
    code 2 waiting · 1 working
    | ) count what is on screen after filtering.

  h2#order How things are ordered
  p
    | The most urgent things come first. Bays are ordered by their most urgent session, then by name. Inside a bay, and
    | in the list, sessions are ordered by status (waiting, then error, then working and compacting, then stale, then
    | idle, then ended), then by their most recent activity.

  h2#live Keeping up to date
  p
    | The Floor updates itself as events arrive, over one live connection to the server. If the connection drops (for
    | example when your phone sleeps), it reconnects by itself and catches up. It also re-checks every 30 seconds as a
    | safety net, so you never need to reload the page.

  h2#empty When the Floor is empty
  p
    | "No sessions today" usually means one of three things: nothing ran today (try
    strong All
    | ), the computer is not paired yet (see
    a(href="/docs/machines") Pairing machines
    | ), or the session was started before pairing and so has no plugin (start a new one). More causes are in
    a(href="/docs/troubleshooting#session-missing") Troubleshooting
    | .
